        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4bb71d4a-3842-5355-bca6-ccb48029bd85",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Fuest, David Wiltse, Sharon Gless, Julie Kavner, Don Johnson, Arthur Hill, Audra Lindley, Peter Maloney\n- Works: Revenge of the Stepford Wives, Miami Vice, Nash Bridges, The Knick, Remember WENN, Gotham, Greetings, Capone, A Little Romance, Hide in Plain Sight, The Children, The Thing, Desperately Seeking Susan, Manhunter, Tune in Tomorrow, JFK, Private Parts, Boiler Room, Requiem for a Dream, K-PAX\n- Roles: James \"Sonny\" Crockett\n- Topics: television acting, film acting\n\nFacts:\n- In 1980, the television film Revenge of the Stepford Wives was directed by Robert Fuest, written by David Wiltse, and starred Sharon Gless, Julie Kavner, Don Johnson, Arthur Hill, and Audra Lindley.\n- In the 1980s, Don Johnson played James \"Sonny\" Crockett in the television series Miami Vice.\n- In 1990, Don Johnson had the title role in the cop series Nash Bridges.\n- Peter Maloney appeared in the films Greetings (1968), Capone (1975), A Little Romance (1979), Hide in Plain Sight (1980), The Children (1980), Revenge of the Stepford Wives (1980), The Thing (1982), Desperately Seeking Susan (1985), Manhunter (1986), Tune in Tomorrow (1990), JFK (1991), Private Parts (1997), Boiler Room (2000), Requiem for a Dream (2000), and K-PAX (2001).\n- Peter Maloney's television credits include The Knick, Remember WENN, and Gotham.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
